{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld","id":1539803,"title":"How deep is the underworld?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-04T15:41:46-07:00","id":1539803,"title":"How deep is the underworld?","content":"how deep is the underworld, and where does it lead to? the lower depths? maybe there are beings similar to the neverborn in the deepest levels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27683-bernese","name":"Bernese","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T17:38:27-07:00","id":1539809,"title":"","content":"Purely for my own satisfaction, I'd say that if you could reach the bottom of the Ocean of Fragments, which you can't, you'd find the Abyss. I have toyed with the idea that far from shore, over the non-horizon from anywhere, there lies an island, a final Dominion, that has something on it that you'd just naturally call a watchtower. And in that tower, there is some lead lying around, or even apeiron, and a tool and die clearly meant for striking coins. It means <i>something</i>, but not as much as anyone might be hoping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T17:56:22-07:00","id":1539810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bernese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld#post1539803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how deep is the underworld, and where does it lead to? the lower depths? maybe there are beings similar to the neverborn in the deepest levels?</div> </div> </div> </div>The deepest levels have an ocean that dissolves identity in it. Whatever's below that, beyond speculation about the Chthonic Gods and chthonians bigger than the ones capable of emerging from the Rivers, is down to speculation.<br /> <br /> The particular nature of the Underworld is such that it's not hard to speculate on there being doors to or entities from the Lower Depths down there, but by and large the Lower Mysteries are the islands of stability between the shores of the Ocean of Fragments and the River Cities at the edge of the Upper Reaches. Chthonians are dead and were never alive, and the deepest Dead Dominions that border the Ocean serve as the main navigational aids for anyone trying to brave the territories of the Admiral and the Leviathan to travel from one shore to another.<br /> <br /> If you want a depth in units of measurement, the place is off-kilter enough that even if getting into the bottom half of the Underworld didn't necessitate travel on the Rivers you're unlikely to get instrumentation all the way down to the Black Beach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T06:52:11-07:00","id":1539851,"title":"","content":"Old Laws of the Island:<br /> Each shall strike once only.<br /> The living shall not abide here.<br /> (Some more recent hand has added &quot;You get about a week. It's too late for us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Any suggestions for a third?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T07:37:04-07:00","id":1539853,"title":"","content":"Given the function of the Underworld seems to be a failsafe for those ghosts who don't manage to pass one (I take it that the reason integrity 10 characters don't leave ghosts is that they pass on automatically) it suggests the ultimate option is for these poor u fortunate entities to enter the Ocean of Fragments, and have all their trauma, all those things that caused them to fail to pass on, everything about you be removed from you... Leaving nothing as you dissolve and finally do get to pass on (maybe).<br /> <br /> The question isn't what is beyond the Ocean, it is what is keeping the Dominions from falling into it and speeding up this recycling process... How deep is it? As deep as it needs to be.<br /> <br /> Does it lead to the lower Depths? I doubt it.<br /> Where does it lead? Presumably it is one step on the path to reincarnation/passing on.<br /> <br /> Chthonians may be similar to the Neverborn the biggest of those entities would be God-like. But what purpose would they serve?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T08:57:30-07:00","id":1539858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539853#post1539853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the function of the Underworld seems to be a failsafe for those ghosts who don't manage to pass one (I take it that the reason integrity 10 characters don't leave ghosts is that they pass on automatically) it suggests the ultimate option is for these poor u fortunate entities to enter the Ocean of Fragments, and have all their trauma, all those things that caused them to fail to pass on, everything about you be removed from you... Leaving nothing as you dissolve and finally do get to pass on (maybe).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a failsafe? I believe that in The Previous Game it was established to <i>have been</i>, but to serve that purpose very poorly now, if at all. Geist definitely says that the ghost is not the person or the person's soul. I have always just assumed - I'm pretty sure this isn't mentioned anywhere - that the ghost passing on is in some Mysterious way good for, or possibly even necessary to, the departed soul, in whatever condition it now exists. Partial dissolution in the Ocean might aid passing on; total dissolution ought in my opinion to be an alternative to passing on, and a terrible one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T09:20:54-07:00","id":1539859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539858#post1539858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it a failsafe? I believe that in The Previous Game it was established to <i>have been</i>, but to serve that purpose very poorly now, if at all. Geist definitely says that the ghost is not the person or the person's soul. I have always just assumed - I'm pretty sure this isn't mentioned anywhere - that the ghost passing on is in some Mysterious way good for, or possibly even necessary to, the departed soul, in whatever condition it now exists. Partial dissolution in the Ocean might aid passing on; total dissolution ought in my opinion to be an alternative to passing on, and a terrible one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is. You can't resolve anchors which have been destroyed, right?<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with The Previous Game?<br /> <br /> The fact that getting to the Ocean requires passing through many challenges and risks getting absorbed into the Underworld itself (running out of essence) does already act as a pretty horrific alternative ending.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it is not a very good failsafe in that case, most ghost don't make it that far. There are no signpost indicating that the should be heading that way - while in the dark era The Sundered World, it mentions Avernian Gates which were originally pools of water, and which lead directly to the Ocean, and then later the first islands emerging from the Ocean.<br /> <br /> Hanging on to those tiny bits of life, struggling to retain your anchors and then your memories, and eventually losing your essence and becoming part of the land of the Underworld is the bad ending.<br /> <br /> The thing that death is supposed to teach...<br /> <br /> At least that is my take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-05-2024, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T09:29:30-07:00","id":1539860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539859#post1539859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not familiar with The Previous Game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure because it was a long time ago and esoteric even then, but I believe that Demon: the Fallen for old World of Darkness established that the Rebels of the Seventh House built the Underworld as a refugee camp for dead humans back when mortality was new. Then they all got locked in their own sub-basement for uncountable time and the whole thing went to crap.<br /> <br /> I've only ever glanced at Sundered World, I'll check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T09:39:52-07:00","id":1539861,"title":"","content":"Ok, no. The Fallen are not part of the CofD setting. Definitely didn't build the Underworld, a lot of that kind of world building is left for the ST at your table to make up answers which work for your game.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is my preference.<br /> <br /> Oh, you could also get eaten by entities in the sea, possibly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T10:40:16-07:00","id":1539864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539861#post1539861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, no. The Fallen are not part of the CofD setting. Definitely didn't build the Underworld, a lot of that kind of world building is left for the ST at your table to make up answers which work for your game.<br /> <br /> My interpretation is my preference.<br /> <br /> Oh, you could also get eaten by entities in the sea, possibly...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, that's why I called it &quot;The Previous Game.&quot;<br /> <br /> I often do this, and should be more careful. I say things that I believe will be five-second riddles, because I think it will be more amusing that way. Then they turn out to be, say, thirty minute riddles, and I end up actually confusing people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T11:55:46-07:00","id":1539869,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not familiar with Wraith or DtF.<br /> <br /> My infering that it is a failsafe is based on how memories work for ghosts.<br /> <br /> They can be traded, ghosts also gain essence if they are remembered as they were while alive (by someone who is still alive), and gain essence from their anchors (which are things they have a deep connection to).<br /> <br /> They are explicitly not the soul, but their initial rank is determined by the integrity of the soul, so they are directly related.<br /> <br /> In Mummy cosmology the soul is five-fold, so you could take it that they represent a part of the soul (and Shades represent another part - namely the shadow). In this case the fact that dopplegangers can exist implies not that these soul Fragments aren't 'the real thing' but that they are all parts of the soul and dopplegangers are a fragment of the part which mummy calls - well, again, imo, Ren - the name.<br /> <br /> I associate the name with the identity which is defined by the memories. And that ties in to the themes around memory built into Geist.<br /> <br /> So washing away those memories, allowing them pass on despite all of the negative experiences that they are holding onto...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:04:01-07:00","id":1539870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539869#post1539869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not familiar with Wraith or DtF.<br /> <br /> My infering that it is a failsafe is based on how memories work for ghosts.<br /> <br /> They can be traded, ghosts also gain essence if they are remembered as they were while alive (by someone who is still alive), and gain essence from their anchors (which are things they have a deep connection to).<br /> <br /> They are explicitly not the soul, but their initial rank is determined by the integrity of the soul, so they are directly related.<br /> <br /> In Mummy cosmology the soul is five-fold, so you could take it that they represent a part of the soul (and Shades represent another part - namely the shadow). In this case the fact that dopplegangers can exist implies not that these soul Fragments aren't 'the real thing' but that they are all parts of the soul and dopplegangers are a fragment of the part which mummy calls - well, again, imo, Ren - the name.<br /> <br /> I associate the name with the identity which is defined by the memories. And that ties in to the themes around memory built into Geist.<br /> <br /> So washing away those memories, allowing them pass on despite all of the negative experiences that they are holding onto...</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I can sort of see it with your further explanation. I'm not sure whether I <i>like</i> it. I'll have to think about it more. I found the section you referred to in Sundered World, and it's interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:14:56-07:00","id":1539871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539870#post1539870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I can sort of see it with your further explanation. I'm not sure whether I <i>like</i> it. I'll have to think about it more. I found the section you referred to in Sundered World, and it's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it doesn't work in your game, don't use it.<br /> <br /> I mean, I am also assuming several things. 1) Passing on is a 'good' ending<br /> 2) Passing on is different from being destroyed in some meaningful sense<br /> 3) Ghosts are actually parts of the soul seperated at death containing the memories (or some of the memories) of the person.<br /> 4) integrity 10 characters that produce no ghost when they die automatically get the 'good' ending.<br /> <br /> - the only thing I can say for certain is that there is a 'good' ending in Geist (at least for player characters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:37:54-07:00","id":1539872,"title":"","content":"I think it's pretty effectively unlimited in depth. It's akin to asking how deep reality is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:46:12-07:00","id":1539873,"title":"","content":"So, that Island:<br /> The Kerberos is pretty much D&amp;D Tiamat, but all in lunar hues. It's generally sleeping, but will wake up <i>fast</i> if anyone breaks a Law. It might actually be Supernal. It's a Mystery. It doesn't impose Conditions, it just eats people.<br /> If you strike a coin - one to a customer, please, and if explorers haven't figured out that &quot;Each may strike once only&quot; refers to striking coins, it would be kind to give them a hint - it has the following effects:<br /> It can be lost, stolen, traded, lent, or given. It's a coin, those are what they're for.<br /> It is a &quot;rare, expensive, or dangerous&quot; prop in <i>any </i>Ceremony where you can work it in. (Try baking into a cake for a Dumb Supper! It's made of minimally-reactive apeiron, it's not <i>that </i>poisonous...)<br /> It is an acceptable deposit at any Irkalla Gate, in lieu of the toll. You'll get it back when you leave, <i>if</i> you don't leave as a fugitive.<br /> It is a Moros Coin tool, but better. Its tool yantra is +2. It can be dedicated, and likely will be. It's likely to be the <i>thing</i> a Moros who despises possessions will be most concerned about.<br /> It is all about legacies, and Legacies. Its tool yantra goes up to +3 if it's used to enhance or reinforce a physical object that has outlasted, or might plausibly outlast, a typical human lifetime. It's also a Coin tool for any Legacy that grants Death as an extra Ruling Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T12:55:51-07:00","id":1539876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539871#post1539871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it doesn't work in your game, don't use it.<br /> <br /> I mean, I am also assuming several things. 1) Passing on is a 'good' ending<br /> 2) Passing on is different from being destroyed in some meaningful sense<br /> 3) Ghosts are actually parts of the soul seperated at death containing the memories (or some of the memories) of the person.<br /> 4) integrity 10 characters that produce no ghost when they die automatically get the 'good' ending.<br /> <br /> - the only thing I can say for certain is that there is a 'good' ending in Geist (at least for player characters).</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Underworld <i>crueler</i>. I think. If I end up preferring your made-up metaphysics rather than my existing made-up metaphysics, I will <i>make</i> it work for my game. Or go back to Wraith and say that Oblivion and Transcendence look the same from the outside, and no one will ever know.<br /> <br /> My current game isn't Geist or Geist-adjacent, it's Hunters in the Hedge - White Hare and Nebula mostly, Ashwood money-man and horrible tourist in everyone else's Very Serious Business. So I won't need an answer right away, and can ruminate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T13:39:08-07:00","id":1539880,"title":"","content":"The Hedge is a pretty bad place to die, tbh. I don't think Hedge Ghosts get to go to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> But if you think the Underworld is nice, you haven't been paying attention.<br /> <br /> Ghosts typically get dragged down there against their will (When their anchors are gone, or reapers come up to get them). <br /> <br /> If they run out of essence (which they no longer have anchors to provide) they end up as horrible clscreaming tableauxs in the walls of the Underworld, so they are forced to find essence.<br /> <br /> If they have survived any length hanging on to their anchors, then most of the people who remember them as they were when they were alive have likely passed or otherwise gotten on with their life, so older ghosts get precious little essence that way.<br /> <br /> Ghosts can prey on each other to get essence, but that is inherently dangerous.<br /> <br /> In the shallow parts, the best way to get essence is spending a few hours each day scavenging the shores of one of the rivers to find castoffs (the ghost of a destroyed object - which without anchors likely gets brought straight to the Underworld) and will not fight back if you try to consume it...<br /> <br /> Overall the river cities are horrible, always bustling for more essence, there is no steady supply, unless...<br /> <br /> You cross one of the rivers and enter the deep dominions. This requires submitting to the Old Laws, you get enough essence per day to survive just by following the Old Laws, but this too is a trap. The Old Laws are typically pretty shitty, some Dominions don't even let people leave.<br /> <br /> Breaking the laws means going up against a Kerebos (likely rank 5 or higher...) These are nigh onto gods, and forced to enforce the Old Laws.<br /> <br /> Going deeper, each Dominion has more laws the more rivers you cross. But, that does assume you can pay the ferryman for passage - probably not too hard, but it may be a challenge.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the rivers, if you try to drink from them there is a non-trivial chance of beig destroyed, but if you succeed you lose yourself, get transformed into a little death god, a monstrous entity barely recognisable as human... A Geist. Is that a win?<br /> <br /> Even assuming you can manage to survive to the Ocean of Fragments without running out of essence or getting trapped in a Deep Dominion, or befalling some other horrible end. There are still the Chtonic beings that live there and the complete absence of knowledge that it is actually the right decision to make (because nobody knows what happens when you pass on...) It could be an entirely neutral ending. Who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T13:51:04-07:00","id":1539881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539880#post1539880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you think the Underworld is nice, you haven't been paying attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld is a bitter trap. The Hedge is a bitter trap too, but it's a <i>fun</i>, <i>cool </i>one. That's how it does the trapping.<br /> The large-scale objective of Geist seems to be <i>making </i>a little piece of the Underworld nice. Ever read a comic called Proposition Player? It's about a gambler who buys some souls, thinking it's a joke, and finds that he really owns them now and as such is an underworld god. Other, bigger, gods try to lean on him. He rooks them all in the end, and creates an afterlife that is merely jerkish and tacky, not monstrously cruel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:13:35-07:00","id":1539884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539880#post1539880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you think the Underworld is nice, you haven't been paying attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant <i>finally </i>and <i>absolutely </i>crueler than your interpretation would suggest. Getting there is cruel enough already, I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T14:44:08-07:00","id":1539886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539881#post1539881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The large-scale objective of Geist seems to be <i>making </i>a little piece of the Underworld nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading of Geist 2e may be conditioned by my reading of Book of the Dead.<br /> Also, I <i>liked</i> Book of the Dead. It gave me an idea for an alternate Sangiovanni bloodline, which I still use sometimes, even if 2e has orphaned it a bit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T17:48:13-07:00","id":1539900,"title":"","content":"I did like the parts of book of the dead that I read.<br /> <br /> But I find most 2e stuff i just better written... Geist is one of the few games which has a possible happy ending. Like you can actually make a difference... The happy endings for Promethean is you get to be human, living in the * of Darkness. I mean sure, free from the downsides of being a Promethean, it's a win, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T18:06:51-07:00","id":1539901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1539803-how-deep-is-the-underworld?p=1539900#post1539900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did like the parts of book of the dead that I read.<br /> <br /> But I find most 2e stuff i just better written... Geist is one of the few games which has a possible happy ending. Like you can actually make a difference... The happy endings for Promethean is you get to be human, living in the * of Darkness. I mean sure, free from the downsides of being a Promethean, it's a win, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e <i>is </i>better. It took me a long time to accept this because of the orphaned stuff. Then I found the orphaned stuff on Storyteller's Vault or did it myself, which was sometimes harder than expected.<br /> I am old, old, old, to this property and its predecessor, but new to this forum and the Storyteller's Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-05-2024, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T13:09:18-07:00","id":1540005,"title":"","content":"I think I've decided that it's not <i>impossible </i>that total dissolution in the Ocean of Fragments will cure what ails you and let you pass on. But I'm going to leave that as a terrifying leap of faith.<br /> <br /> A long time a ago I read a review of that movie Ghost with Demi Moore and Patrick Swayze that said no one would ever turn down heaven to haunt, which I can get behind. But Swayze, when he turns down heaven, clearly <i>doesn't know what he's doing</i>, which changes everything. The movie is not the game, but...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T11:40:57-08:00","id":1556177,"title":"","content":"In my games? The Lower Depths. Once all identifiers're gone, a ghost drops through, utterly without form and awareness, into a random Lower Depth, which leads to a variety of fates (consumption, torment, transforming into something new).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}